"In Artonan magic, chaos means demons; high-chaos areas breed demon outbreaks."
"Worlds track a chaos index; outbreak forecasts read like weather reports."
"High chaos degrades a world's System, and replacing it while chaos remains does more harm."
"The System bars low-rank Avowed from high-chaos zones, rating each one's susceptibility."
"Susceptibility means risk of demonic incursion and loss of one's assignment."
"Teleports into high-chaos places use an older, magically violent method."
"The violent teleport is too dangerous for average people and easier with good infrastructure."
"An Avowed's presence stabilizes System calls made from a high-chaos world."
"Chaos behaves like bad weather on an afflicted world and disturbs the local System."
"In a chaos-driven System failure translation garbles and the interface turns to alien symbols."
"Such a failure cuts teleports, calls and the Wardrobe, though a skill's halo can persist."
"Chaos maps show zones in purple, pink and red like weather radar, updating every 16 minutes."
"Red is not the worst chaos level; other places are far worse than a red zone."
"The worst chaos comes from things out of a broken dimension."
"Next worst are beings of high authority who magnify and spread the chaos they meet."
"Chaos morphs living things faster and more visibly than non-living ones."
"A body struck by chaos morphs through person, plant, rot and emptiness."
"Avowed and wizards resist chaos through their authority; others die first."
"Only wizard ships from the Mother can clear a chaos zone; the Artonan language has six words for chaos."
"Chaos destroys the way of things but is also shaped by it; Artonans are far from predicting it."
"Reality has strength: chaos damages it, yet reality still acts on demons."
